    "descriptions": {
      "en": {
        "tagline": "Statically typed systems programming language unifying Single-Level Store (SLS), Z3 SMT verification, and causal mesh networks.",
        "summary": "Engine Lang is an open, unowned systems programming language designed to abolish the memory-disk duality through hardware-direct Single-Level Store (SLS), mathematical proof of invariants via Z3 SMT solver, and native causal graph replication.",
        "text": "Engine Lang (engine / .eng) eliminates the traditional fragmentation of enterprise infrastructure by collapsing the application layer, ORM, database, cache, message broker, and vector index into a single verifiable compilation unit. Built under the Apache 2.0 license as a sovereign public good."
      }
    }
  },
